    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe whole idea of the `treesitter` target in 'mini.bracketed' is that it is designed to work *without* any queries. So although I can see the appeal, this is out of scope for 'mini.bracketed'.\n\nThe alternative is to use ['mini.ai' tree-sitter textobjects](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-ai.html#miniai.gen_spec.treesitter) in combination with [`MiniAi.move_cursor()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-ai.html#miniai.move_cursor) (or using default `g[` and `g]` to move to being/end of the textobject).",
            "created_at": "2025-11-13T18:18:14Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2114#issuecomment-3529104775",
